// Bot chat lines, medieval and funny.
//
// Every line is a joke, and short.  The winners insult the loser, and the losers make fun of themselves.
// Same arrays and topics as the old Darkest Dungeon set this replaced (still in git history).
// Add or remove lines freely, just keep the array size matching the line count.

string quotes_connect[40] = {
    "Hark! I arrive, and onions arrive with me.",
    "Make way! A knight comes, his horse already left.",
    "Bow before me, peasants, or step over the puddle.",
    "Behold the hero of nine villages, all mine mother's.",
    "I have the strength of ten men, all sickly.",
    "I slew dragons once. In a barn. They were chickens.",
    "Fetch thy bravest man. Then fetch a mop.",
    "Thy village called. They want their sheep back.",
    "Draw thy blade, knave. Or thy spoon, I'm easy.",
    "Who wishes to be humiliated first? Form a queue.",
    "The prophecy foretold a hero. I arrived instead.",
    "Stand aside, thou turnip with a sword.",
    "I have ridden far and smell of it. So shalt thou.",
    "Gather round, ye dolts, greatness is half off.",
    "Good morrow, scoundrels. Who owes me twelve groats?",
    "I bring death, taxes, and a loud stomach.",
    "Mine armor shineth and thy chances are in a ditch.",
    "Thou lookest like a pie that lost a bet.",
    "Tremble, ye pox-ridden pigeons! Or at least shoo.",
    "Which of ye is my sparring dummy today?",
    "I am here, and mine mother is not proud, as usual.",
    "A knight, a fool, a bard: I am the middle one.",
    "Do not mind the smell. 'Tis mine armor. And me.",
    "I come to defend the realm, and to find the privy.",
    "Let the heralds announce me. Failing that, a cough.",
    "Behold! A hero, as seen on mine own sign.",
    "I bring a sword, a shield, and no plan whatsoever.",
    "Who wants to die first? I accept volunteers.",
    "I am told the dungeon has free ale. I was lied to.",
    "Good morrow! Let us begin the stabbing.",
    "I come in peace. Mostly. The peace expires soon.",
    "Pardon me, I seem to have wandered into glory.",
    "Hail! I have been ordered to fight thee. Sorry.",
    "By royal decree, I'm to smite thee. I shall try.",
    "Thou art all surrounded by me. I'm one man, but loud.",
    "Yield now and I'll only mildly stab thee.",
    "My blade is sharp, my wit duller, my courage on loan.",
    "I have come far to be rude to thee. Well met.",
    "Fetch the priest. Or the barber. I'm not picky.",
    "The tavern was closed, so I came here to hurt thee.",
};

string quotes_welcome[36] = {
    "Welcome! Thou hast the face of a man who loses at dice.",
    "Well met! Thy mother must despair of thy trousers.",
    "Fresh peasant! Mind the knives, they are for thee.",
    "Hail, thou sack of regret. Wipe thy boots on thyself.",
    "Enter freely. The exits are for winners.",
    "Lovely armor. Pity about the man inside.",
    "Thou smellest of cheese and defeat. Welcome!",
    "A new face! I shall remember it, then rearrange it.",
    "Pull up a stump and be humiliated by professionals.",
    "Thou art welcome here, as a boil is welcome.",
    "Another volunteer! We were low on punching bags.",
    "Welcome! We shall send flowers to thy burial early.",
    "Hail, thou walking cautionary tale.",
    "Greetings, noble fool. Mind the floor, 'tis thy kin.",
    "Ah, thou art here. We were enjoying ourselves.",
    "Welcome! Thou lookest healthy. We shall fix that.",
    "Newcomer! May thy dagger be sharp, unlike thee.",
    "A warm welcome to our newest corpse.",
    "Welcome! Wipe thy feet on the dead, as is custom.",
    "Another soul! The pit was getting lonely.",
    "Greetings! Try not to die on the rug, 'tis new.",
    "Well met, goodman! Thy face is familiar. Plain.",
    "Thou art late, and yet no less doomed.",
    "Welcome, friend. Thou hast the look of a snack.",
    "Ah, a guest! We shall serve thee lead.",
    "Hail! The last fellow lasted a whole minute. Beat that.",
    "Come in! Thy grave is already dug. Nice, aye?",
    "New blood! The old blood is getting boring.",
    "Hello, stranger. Dost thou have a will? Just asking.",
    "Greetings! Thy armor fits well, for a corpse.",
    "Behold, a challenger! A poor one, but still.",
    "Welcome! Thou lookest like thou hast lost thy mother.",
    "Hail! Pay no heed to the screaming. 'Tis a local custom.",
    "Another brave one! Brave being a polite word.",
    "Come, sit, die. In that order, ideally.",
    "Pleased to meet thee! Do not get attached.",
};

string quotes_victory[44] = {
    "Thou fightest like a milkmaid with a grievance.",
    "Mine apologies, I thought thou wert the dummy.",
    "Back to the mud, thou bog-born blunderer!",
    "Thy father smelt of elderberries. Also, I won.",
    "Another peasant parted from his limbs. Tuesday.",
    "Is that thy valor? I've seen braver turnips.",
    "Rest in pieces, thou festering crumpet.",
    "Thou dost die as thou livest: loudly, no plan.",
    "Thy skill is a joke, and not a funny one.",
    "A disappointing foe. Mine sword fell asleep.",
    "Hark, the bells! Oh, 'tis thy dignity tolling.",
    "Flee not, coward! Oh, thou art dead. Carry on.",
    "Pray forgive the mess. Thou wert so juicy.",
    "Another pelt for my wall of poor decisions.",
    "Thou hast the spirit of a wet scone.",
    "Down thou goest, thou pestilent pudding!",
    "I'd give a eulogy, but I'm busy winning.",
    "Thou diest like a goose in a mood. Honking.",
    "One fewer fool in the realm. No thanks needed.",
    "Thy head shall make a fine paperweight.",
    "Do try for a better face next time.",
    "Slain by a man who owes his tailor. Reflect.",
    "Thou fightest like thou dost shave: badly.",
    "I've slain a thousand, and none put up less of a fight.",
    "Thy corpse shall serve as a lesson. Of what, I'm unsure.",
    "Dead again? Thou makest it look so easy.",
    "Thou hast the grace of a drunk pig on ice.",
    "Behold, thy blood is nearly the color of thy cowardice.",
    "Thy mother weeps. Thy father has left.",
    "Surrender is for those who haven't died yet. Too late.",
    "A noble death? Nay. A clumsy, ridiculous one.",
    "Next time, try to hit me. It's customary.",
    "That felt less like a fight and more like a chore.",
    "Was it meant to be that easy? Do tell the lord.",
    "Stay down, thou noodle! Aye, like that.",
    "Thy sword was lovely. Pity about the hands.",
    "Another victory! Another stain on mine tunic.",
    "Thou wert never a threat, merely a smell.",
    "Thy bones shall make a fine soup. Not mine, mind.",
    "Hast thou considered farming? Thou'rt dreadful at this.",
    "I'd salute thee, but thou'rt in pieces.",
    "Thou art defeated! Gloriously, and by a nobody.",
    "That's how it's done. Take notes. Oh, thou'rt dead.",
    "Thou stinkest of failure, and also fish.",
};

string quotes_deathsdoor[36] = {
    "'Tis but a scratch! The size of a ham, but a scratch.",
    "I have lost mine arm. Nay, 'tis hiding.",
    "Mine armor was not rated for this many holes.",
    "Mine insides are outside. A bold fashion choice.",
    "Is this blood mine? I don't recall owning this much.",
    "Merciful heavens, I'm leaking in front of guests.",
    "Fetch a physician. Or a mop. Both, ideally.",
    "I feel strangely light. I blame the missing parts.",
    "Hold thy fire! I need a moment to be dramatic.",
    "Tell my wife I love her. And I owe the blacksmith.",
    "My spleen just left for better employment.",
    "It hurts exactly as much as it looks.",
    "If I perish, bury me with mine honor. I lost it.",
    "Death knocketh. I'm pretending to be out.",
    "My legs have filed for separation.",
    "Aye, I've seen worse. On others. From afar.",
    "Brave Sir Me is in a spot of bother. A large spot.",
    "I'm not afraid of death, just of the screaming.",
    "I may be dying, but I look splendid doing it.",
    "Mine health is low and mine mood is lower.",
    "The reaper hath me by the elbow, and he's polite.",
    "I've got a bit of everything missing. Mostly blood.",
    "Pray, hurry, I'm bleeding on the good carpet.",
    "Is there a doctor? Or a priest? Or a mop?",
    "I can see the light, and it appears quite rude.",
    "My blood is leaving without saying goodbye.",
    "Good news: I'm not dead yet. Bad news: also true.",
    "Someone's stabbed me. I have strong opinions on that.",
    "I've seen the inside of a man. 'Twas me. Unpleasant.",
    "My last will: I leave my debts to my enemies.",
    "I have been better. Specifically, yesterday.",
    "Mine arms are tired. Mostly from holding my guts.",
    "Death hath scheduled me for noon. I'm early.",
    "I've a feeling I'm dying. Either that or lunch.",
    "Tell me, does this look fatal? Asking for a friend.",
    "Mine spirit is willing. Mine spleen is not.",
};

string quotes_death[44] = {
    "Alas, slain by a peasant. In front of company.",
    "Tell my horse I died bravely. He won't believe thee.",
    "Mine honor is dead. It went first, nobody noticed.",
    "Woe! I perished like a man who forgot to duck.",
    "Mine armor was clearly made by a man who hated me.",
    "They shall write songs of this. All cruel.",
    "I died as I lived: confidently wrong.",
    "I forgot to block. Entirely. At all. Ever.",
    "Woe is me! Also, ow. Mostly ow.",
    "Mine epitaph: tried his best, hardly.",
    "Farewell, cruel realm. I was bad at thee.",
    "I shall return in an hour, equally terrible.",
    "Bury me face down, to hide how badly I did.",
    "Mother said I'd end up in the ground. Not like this.",
    "Forsooth, I was bested by something frankly rude.",
    "The worms shall dine on mine pride. Plenty there.",
    "I regret nothing, except my entire career.",
    "Mine sword betrayed me. It was sharp, I was not.",
    "Come, sweet death. These legs were decorative.",
    "They said I'd die with a sword in hand. Wrong end.",
    "Tell the lord I fell with a very silly face.",
    "Curse my left hand, for it knoweth not the right.",
    "Well, that was embarrassing. For us both.",
    "I was winning. In mine head. Entirely there.",
    "The last thing I saw was a very rude man.",
    "Woe! I have died, and with such a handsome face.",
    "Mine mother hath warned me about this. Repeatedly.",
    "Dying is easy. Dying with dignity? Not so much.",
    "I'll be back. Probably. If I find mine sword.",
    "Why does it always hurt more than the pamphlet said?",
    "Mine funeral shall be small. Mostly debtors.",
    "Slain by a fool! I'm the greater fool.",
    "I hath been slain. Do give me a moment to sulk.",
    "It was the sun. In mine eyes. In a cave.",
    "Ah well. At least I'll look good in the coffin.",
    "Somebody tell the bard I need a better ending.",
    "Death by peasant. Mine ancestors are mortified.",
    "I blame the cheese. And the peasant. And mostly me.",
    "Mine armor was fine. 'Twas the man inside who failed.",
    "I always said I'd die doing what I loved: losing.",
    "Fie on thee, thou unfair and handsome killer.",
    "What a pity. I was just beginning to warm up.",
    "Mine coin purse is on mine belt. Take it. Go. Leave.",
    "I need a better class of sword. And a better class of me.",
};

string quotes_team[40] = {
    "Stand behind me, thou beloved sacks of useless.",
    "Fear not, brothers! Fear me, I am worse at this.",
    "Charge! I shall follow, from another county.",
    "Keep close, in front, where the arrows are.",
    "Fall in, men of dubious bathing.",
    "Press on! The enemy shall laugh themselves to death.",
    "Mine shield is thy shield. Mine shame is thine too.",
    "Together we are mighty. Alone, thou art a liability.",
    "Worry not. I have a plan. It involveth thy sacrifice.",
    "A team is only as strong as its wisest. I'm elsewhere.",
    "Cover mine back, noble dolt. With thy body, if needed.",
    "Together forever, or until someone dies. Thee.",
    "Keep thy head up. It holds thy helmet on.",
    "Strength in numbers! Mostly thine.",
    "I trust thee with my life. Take no pride in that.",
    "Comrade, I shall try not to cut thee. No promises.",
    "Courage, friend! Or the look of it, in thy case.",
    "We fight as one! I am the one who stays back.",
    "Hold the line, men! I'll hold the rear. And a pastry.",
    "Steady, lads. If we die, I get thy boots.",
    "Allies! I have a plan. It is called: thou first.",
    "Be brave, friends! I shall be brave later.",
    "Let us advance as one! I'll be second.",
    "Whoever dies first gets the good boots.",
    "Spread out, so the arrows kill us one at a time.",
    "If thou seest a monster, run. It's worked so far.",
    "Stay close, but not too close. Thou smellest.",
    "Keep thy shield high and thy standards low.",
    "I'll guard the rear. It's a very important rear.",
    "Fear nothing! That's what I tell the enemy.",
    "Together we shall fall, and in an orderly fashion.",
    "I am thy friend, thy ally, and also hungry.",
    "We'll win, or we'll lie down very convincingly.",
    "Let us fight like heroes, or at least like men.",
    "Forward, brave comrades! Mind the pit. I'll watch.",
    "Thou fightest well! Compared to thy horse.",
    "If we lose, I was never here. Nod politely.",
    "I shall lead! Let us all follow me, from behind.",
    "Teammates! I'll try not to hit thee. Reality varies.",
    "Remember, aim at the enemy. The big one. Not me.",
};

string quotes_suicide[34] = {
    "Behold, I have slain myself. Peak competence.",
    "Mine own hand betrayed me. It was ever a scoundrel.",
    "I fell upon mine sword. It was slippery.",
    "Let history record I was mine own greatest threat.",
    "Gravity: one. Sir Me: nil.",
    "I tripped on my cape. Do not laugh. Fine, laugh.",
    "Woe! Mine hand slipped. As did the rest of me.",
    "I meant to do that. Honest. Hmm, no.",
    "A fatal error, nobly executed by an ignoble man.",
    "Edges are dangerous. Noted. Too late.",
    "A new low in the history of me.",
    "It seemed a good idea. So do most of mine ideas.",
    "I regret to inform thee that I am an idiot.",
    "The ground came from below, as is its custom.",
    "That was meant for thee. I misjudged the geometry.",
    "Tell mine enemies a most dangerous man did this. Me.",
    "Mine greatest enemy is me. Efficiently dispatched.",
    "I wished to nap, and the floor obliged.",
    "Behold, my greatest victory: me, versus me.",
    "A tragic accident. I'm tragic, it's an accident.",
    "I stand corrected. And then I fell.",
    "The pit and I had a disagreement. It won.",
    "I thought that was a door. It was not.",
    "I've killed a thousand foes. This one was smarter.",
    "Do not judge me. Gravity is cheating.",
    "My greatest enemy is stairs. And I'm his friend.",
    "Mine foot found the edge before mine eyes did.",
    "That was a short career. The coffin is brief.",
    "Let that be a lesson to me: don't.",
    "Hark! I've found a new way to lose.",
    "I am my own worst enemy. And my best shot.",
    "I am a fool, and I have the death to prove it.",
    "I did it on purpose. For science. It hurt.",
    "Tell no one. If asked, a monster did it.",
};

string quotes_ridicule[40] = {
    "Thy swordplay needeth a miracle.",
    "Dost thou hold the weapon by the sharp end?",
    "Thou aimest like a blind man tossing hay.",
    "I've seen better aim from a drunk goose.",
    "Fie! Thou art as dangerous as a sleeping hen.",
    "Thy valor is exceeded only by thy stupidity.",
    "Even the village idiot thinks thou art slow.",
    "Thou fightest like thy mother. She's quite good.",
    "Thy skill is so poor the bards refuse to mock it.",
    "Thy weapon weepeth for the hands it serves.",
    "The only thing thou slayest is the mood.",
    "Flee, thou milksop! No, wait, that's thy best idea.",
    "Another miss! A tribute to being bad.",
    "Thou art the reason the realm hath standards.",
    "Is that a sword, or art thou happy to see me?",
    "Please continue. I haven't laughed since the plague.",
    "Thou swingest like a door in a gale.",
    "Thy mother was a good sport about thy father.",
    "Stand still! Let me miss thee properly, to compare.",
    "Thou shamest thy ancestors, and their horses.",
    "Is that a battle cry, or art thou clearing thy throat?",
    "Thou holdest a sword like a fish holds a bicycle.",
    "My horse hath more courage. And a better chin.",
    "Thou art a fine example of what not to be.",
    "Thy blow tickled. Do it again, I laughed.",
    "Thy shield is merely a decorative plate.",
    "I've met bigger threats at bake sales.",
    "Thou fightest like a toddler with a spoon.",
    "Thy sword arm is fine. Thy arm's owner is not.",
    "Is thy armor made of cheese? It smells of it.",
    "Whence came thee? The fool's academy?",
    "Thou hast the finesse of a falling anvil.",
    "I'd kill thee, but I'd feel bad. For about a second.",
    "Thou swingest like thou'rt shooing flies.",
    "Thy plan hath the strategic depth of a puddle.",
    "Even thy shadow is trying to leave thee.",
    "Cease, brave fool! Thou'rt embarrassing us both.",
    "Thy fighting skills are the stuff of nightmares. Mine.",
    "Thou art as threatening as a wet sock.",
    "Fie! Thou fightest like my sister. She wins.",
};

string quotes_intermission_positive[36] = {
    "Victory is mine! Bow, ye also-rans, and hold my coat.",
    "Hearken and weep: the champion hath triumphed.",
    "Let bards sing: I beat thee all, quite handily.",
    "Behold the victor, and thy defeat. Admire both.",
    "Hail to the winner! Sorry, I meant me.",
    "Thou fought bravely, if bravely meaneth badly.",
    "To the victor, spoils. To thee, my pity.",
    "I came, I saw, I made thee look foolish. Again.",
    "Remember this day, losers. Thou wert eclipsed.",
    "Rejoice! Or stop sulking, 'tis unbecoming.",
    "Mine deeds are legend. Thine are an apology.",
    "Back to thy hovels. I shall eat thy share.",
    "A fine battle. For me. For thee, a lesson.",
    "Thy defeat was delicious. I shall have seconds.",
    "Another triumph for the righteous and the handsome.",
    "I'm the champion! Did I mention? Thrice. Because I can.",
    "Hold thy applause, lest I mistake it for pity.",
    "Thou lost most gracefully, for a pile of mud.",
    "Bow, lesser men! The champion hath been crowned.",
    "We won! By which I mean I won, and thou watched.",
    "Hear me, losers: I was magnificent. As always.",
    "Call the bards! Tell them I was spectacular.",
    "Another day, another crown. Thou'st none.",
    "A victory for the ages, or at least the afternoon.",
    "The mud tastes sweet, when it is thy mud.",
    "I'd shake hands, but they're bloody. Some thine.",
    "Weep not, losers. Or do, I enjoy it.",
    "Thy defeat was well executed. By me.",
    "Behold! I have conquered! The hill. And thee.",
    "Gather, ye lesser warriors, and learn from me.",
    "Mine victory is yours too! Pardon, I misspoke. No.",
    "Tonight we feast! Thou shalt watch.",
    "Take solace, vanquished: you made me look good.",
    "Glory is mine, and I wear it humbly. Not really.",
    "Thou wert almost a worthy foe. Almost.",
    "I'm so good, I scare myself. Mostly the stabbing.",
};

string quotes_intermission_negative[36] = {
    "Alas, I was routed. By children, I assume.",
    "Let it be known that I tried. Somewhat.",
    "I fought valiantly. I fought, then I fell.",
    "Mine honor is in ruins, matching mine armor.",
    "A close contest. For the winner, easy.",
    "I call it a draw, in which I am dead.",
    "I lost because of the weather. And skill. Weather.",
    "My shame is plenty and my talent scarce.",
    "I was the weakest of us. May I leave by the back?",
    "By mine troth, I am bad at this.",
    "I'll be better next time. I say that every time.",
    "The sorriest knight in the land, and it's competitive.",
    "Let us never speak of it. Or kindly, with wine.",
    "I retire to weep into mine armor. It's dented.",
    "Mine ancestors roll in their graves. With laughter.",
    "I came for glory and left with a rash.",
    "Next time I'll bring a sword. Or a better me.",
    "We lost, but I looked good doing it. From afar.",
    "Another defeat! At least I'm consistent.",
    "We lost, but at least nobody saw. Right? Right?",
    "Mine honor needs a nap. And a patch.",
    "I'd say I was robbed. But no one robbed me. I just lost.",
    "Pray for me. Preferably loudly, and quickly.",
    "It was a fine battle. For the other fellows.",
    "I'd blame the others, but they were great.",
    "Mine armor squeaked the whole time. That's mine excuse.",
    "We were outnumbered. By skill, mostly.",
    "Do not look at me. I am hideous with shame.",
    "Tell the king I did mine best. He'll sigh.",
    "I hath tasted defeat. It tastes of mine boots.",
    "We lost, but not as badly as I feared. Slightly worse.",
    "Perhaps tomorrow. Or next week. Or never.",
    "I think I fought a bear. It was a child. A big child.",
    "Mine sword and I are both disappointed.",
    "Let us blame the cat. We don't have a cat.",
    "We lost with honor. Mine honor, being very small.",
};
